  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Questionnaire Sheet",
    "overview": "The promo page is a printed survey questionnaire about questionnaires. A single cool white sheet sits on a pale blue desk; everything printed on it in advance (boxes, rules, question numbers, field labels, tints, arrows) is in drop-out form blue, the ink a scanner is meant to ignore, and everything that is an answer or an entry is near-black. Sections are numbered questions with a filled number box on the left, a body in the middle and a margin column of skip instructions on the right that are real in-page links.\n\nThe system is flat, ruled and square. Depth is the sheet lifting off the desk and nothing else. Colour carries meaning, not decoration: blue is the form, black is what was written on it, and red is reserved for exactly one thing, a real change in a question's wording. Archivo is the only text face, worked across its width axis: condensed caps for form labels, a wide heavy cut for the wordmark, a slightly narrowed bold for questions. JetBrains Mono appears only where the reader would type or recognise a literal: commands and variable names.\n\nThis page is a different visual world from the generated history page (`docs/history.html`), which keeps its own older look. The two surfaces share only the mark meanings: red dot = real change, grey ring = cosmetic change, an outer black ring = checked by hand, and a hatched band = the 2021 redesign break.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One sheet, one form ink (blue), one entry ink (near-black), one meaning-bearing accent (red).",
      "Square corners everywhere except answer bubbles (circles) and a 2px hairline on buttons and command blocks.",
      "Structure is drawn with rules and boxes (1.5px form-blue rules, 1px light form lines), never with cards or shadows.",
      "Archivo's width axis does the typographic work; size and weight stay in a narrow band.",
      "Every section reads as a numbered question with a margin of skip instructions."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Red Rule",
        "body": "Real-change red marks a real change in a question's wording and is used for nothing else: not for errors, emphasis, buttons, links or hover states. Its tints exist only around a red dot.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Drop-out Ink Rule",
        "body": "Anything printed before the reader arrives (structure, labels, numbers, instructions, navigation) is form blue; anything that is data or an answer is ink. If an element is blue, it must be part of the form.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Width Axis Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy is expressed through Archivo's width axis first (70 for labels, 80 for numerals, 85 for questions, 100 for text, 125 for the wordmark), weight second, size last. Do not add a second sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Literal Mono Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono is only for text the reader could type or search: commands, variable names, round codes. Never for labels or decoration.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Sheet Rule",
        "body": "There is one raised surface, the sheet. Nothing on it floats: no cards, no lifted panels, no hover elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** draw every printed structure (rules, boxes, labels, numbers, arrows, instructions) in form blue and every entry in ink.",
      "**Do** keep red for real changes only, with its row tint and highlight only around a red dot.",
